{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792302314,"nonce":"D8XcQhfSnAkxc0KGJH3ebFzQy0s=","title":"Python: a typed list of instances made dynamic cannot be appended to","message":"A kinded list literal of instances keeps its typed kind (pointer elements) even when it escapes as a dynamic value. The dynamic method dispatcher then has no arm for that kind, so `append` raises AttributeError:\n\n    class Base(object):\n        def __init__(self, n): self.n = n\n    class Sub(Base): pass\n    def pick(flag):\n        xs = [Sub(1)]\n        if flag:\n            return xs\n        return [1, 2]\n    ys = pick(True)\n    ys.append(Sub(5))     # zypy: AttributeError: 'list' object has no attribute 'append'\n\n`py$call$append$1` handles the i64, f64, str and dynamic list kinds, arrays, and lists of tuples and lists (`elem_lists()`), but not the pointer kind of instance lists or Num lists. Even with an arm, a dynamic append into a pointer-kind list could put an instance of another class under readers typed for one class. A list that can escape to dynamic code should be stored dynamically, or converted when it escapes, as followed unkinded lists already are through `kept`. Kinded literals are not followed.\n\nThis also blocks following a parameter alias (`todo = sources` in deltablue, 71d634e). With the alias, a typed list reached `add_constraints_consuming_to(coll: Object)` and failed this way.","files":null}]}